  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Consists of two sheets, each vertically folded accordion-style and affixed the the front and back covers in tête-bêche style. When unfolded each forms a long single vertical strip approximately 4.25 meters in height and 20 cm in width. One strip contains the poem hand-written in English, the other in Spanish. Four pages of color illustrations are bound with string between the folded strips.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Materials used include white and brown paper of varying textures and weights, sawdust, textiles, stones, and seashells. The covers are made from black roofing paper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="546" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">English and Spanish.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="546" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The poem was previously published in English in the journal "Cuban Studies," volume 42, 2011, pp. 186-195.</subfield>
  </datafield>
